  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Very large volunteer army (~1.2 million) facing two fronts: the Line of Control with Pakistan and the Line of Actual Control with China. Decades of counter-insurgency in Jammu and Kashmir and the North-East. Doctrine moving to Integrated Battle Groups, 'Rudra' all-arms brigades and drone-heavy 'Bhairav' light commando battalions after the May 2025 India-Pakistan conflict (Operation Sindoor), which featured missile, drone and artillery exchanges.",
    "squad_size": 10,
    "fireteam": "Infantry section of 10 with LMG group and rifle group; Rashtriya Rifles counter-insurgency teams. Game: 8 in four pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Cordon-and-search counter-insurgency operations in mountain villages",
      "High-altitude defence and patrolling (Ladakh, Siachen)",
      "Artillery duels and drone strikes across the LoC",
      "Mechanised strikes in the desert (Rajasthan) with T-90S and BMP-2",
      "Special forces (Para SF) cross-border raids and hostage rescue"
    ],
